            "review_text": "majellagomes2015\nMalaysia10 contributions\n0\nDelicious introduction to local cuisine\nJan 2016 • Family\nAngel Palace's menu is not just delectable, it is excellent value for money. I don't know any other place where two people can have a full meal for US$6 - at least, not for the quality, quantity and taste we had. Although there are several cafes and restaurants in the Hang Bong area, the weather was cold and rainy and we could not get out and about as much as we wanted to. But the Angel Palace restaurant did not disappoint. What we liked was the freshness of the ingredients and the simple, uncluttered culinary methods that could produce such outstanding flavours. I had very little knowledge of Vietnamese cuisine before going to Hanoi but I am an ardent fan of it now! Everything we ordered came freshly and skillfully prepared, and beautifully presented, with perfectly balanced flavours - served by the most hardworking, courteous, welcoming and cheerful staff I have ever had the good fortune to encounter!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 8, 2016",
